A||||7||stomper282||Someone hit me with a cluex4 !||||5||
Z||000000||stomper282||12-21-2000||01:49 AM||||I justbought a 88 Fiero GT, I have owned 2 84 Fiero's. My car is registered as a 87, My vin # reads as an 88. Can some one clue me in on how to tell the differance? Mostly becuase I'm trying to lower it! I have springs on order for an 87, will they work? <BR> I am also looking for Info on coil over's for it so far I've come up with nothing(and then some). <BR> On a diffrent note I work for America's tire/Discount tire Co. so any tire info you guys/gals need I'm here for you!!!<BR> I am curently running 18's on my car, I'm soon to be custom widend to 18x9 in the rear so I can run a 265/35-18. <BR>         Thanks ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||12-21-2000||01:56 AM||||Here's a quick check, Are your brake rotors solid or vented? (Check fronts)<BR>Solid = 87<BR>Vented = 88<P>87 suspension parts are not interchangable with 88 suspension parts.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stomper282||12-21-2000||02:05 AM||||My rotors are solid, do all 88 come stock with vented rotors?<BR>        ||||reg||5
Z||000003||Oreif||12-21-2000||02:14 AM||||Yes, all 88's are vented. The entire brake system (rotors/calipers) and suspension are different for 88's.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||12-21-2000||06:11 AM||||Sounds like you have a very late year 87?<P>18s???? Depending on the wheel style you have I have always hated the open faced style wheels. They make the brakes and rotors seem so freaking small as to be embarrassing...<P>(puts his two pennies down.) Thank you!<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 12-21-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000005||1FST2M6||12-21-2000||11:12 AM||||Welcome to the forum!<P><BR>18s are nice but tires are a B!tch to get if you in the mountains and thrash one... 17s are everywhere! <P>(current ride) <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstlow.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstlow.jpg</A>  17x9s(r) 17x7(f) I think i bought a set of Konig GT-Rs from you guys in january of 98.!   <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/travis.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/travis.jpg</A>  (former ride)<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||12-22-2000||08:26 AM||||the model year changeover is usually in late september or october. you prob got one assembled between then and january. so its a 88 model, manufactured before the end of the year so technicaly its an 87. Check the sticker on door -has actual date of manufacture. common practice to use remaining supply of previous year parts. My Mercedes was titled as a 1972, date of manufacture 11/71 all the brake parts were all  71 which like Fiero were all completely different in 72 model. RV industry does same thing and always calls these 'bastards' by SPECIAL EDITION.||||reg||7
Z||000007||stomper282||12-22-2000||09:32 PM||||Thank you guys for the info, it realy clears things up for me!!! <BR>            Mike.||||reg||6
